WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.790
So Last Friday, the progressive website Mother
Jones included me in an article about a quote

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:15.940
"new extremist media industry that is further
to the right than Breitbart."

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:20.360
In the piece, the author referred to me as
"far right", citing interviews I've done with

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:25.300
Mike Cernovich, Milo Yiannopoulos and Lauren
Southern to back up his accusation.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.269
He cherry picked these guests to fit his narrative,
yet somehow missing the endless amount of

00:00:29.269 --> 00:00:35.070
liberals I've had on and the progressives
I've hosted, including Margaret Cho, Hillary

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.680
Rosen, Mark Duplass, John Fugelsang and Michael
Ian Black.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:44.519
The article also attacked Patreon, the crowdfunding
platform of which myself and my team's livelihood

00:00:44.519 --> 00:00:51.360
depends on, for being tolerant of people with
far right views such as mine, though of course,

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.100
nowhere did it include any of my purported
"far right" views.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:00.360
Earlier in the week, Forbes called The Rubin
Report a "conservative talk show", but immediately

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.160
retracted the statement when I contacted them.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.830
Ironically, I've been saying for awhile defending
my liberal beliefs is becoming a conservative

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:08.970
position.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:14.220
Although I don't think being called a conservative
is somehow bad, it clearly isn't a proper

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:19.230
descriptor for this show in which I've hosted
people from across the political divide.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:24.810
For Mother Jones to accuse me of being an
extremist, further to the right of Breitbart,

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:29.630
is obviously an inflammatory and demonstrably
dishonest statement.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.250
I've been around many people who over the
last few years have been unfairly maligned,

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.930
and I'm all to familiar with how this all
goes.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:41.480
Whether it's Sam Harris, Jordan Petersen,
Colin Moriarty or Brett Weinstein -- each

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:46.720
attack is virtually never based on what these
people have said, but are instead crafted

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:51.320
out of straw man arguments with the words
racist and bigot tossed around like candy.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:58.270
Suddenly, the onus is on people who aren't
racists or bigots to disprove this accusation,

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:03.060
usually slung by a misguided celebrity, or
a malicious newspaper or website.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:08.360
The move, then, is on the accused -- should
they spend time and energy defending themselves

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:14.360
from accusations which aren't true, only to
bring more attention to the accusations themselves?

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:18.520
Or should they ignore ignore them, hoping
the false claims will go away over time.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:22.920
I think there are solid arguments to be made
for either tactic, and it truly depends on

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:26.020
the situation at hand and the person involved.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.709
In this case, though, I went on the attack.

00:02:28.709 --> 00:02:36.000
I decided this case was too egregious to ignore,
contacting the article's author via Twitter,

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.060
screenshotting pieces of his article and asking
him to defend them.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:44.200
Of course, he couldn't defend his own words...that's
the thing with truth, it's hard to work around...and

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:48.901
eventually he made slight changes to the article,
like including a tweet of mine in which I

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:55.540
defended myself from his claims, and he removing
the word "far" in front of the word "right"

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.770
before referencing me in the article.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:03.121
Putting aside the specifics of this article
itself, I was happy to get a strong defense

00:03:03.121 --> 00:03:06.599
in public from many friends all over the political
map.

00:03:06.599 --> 00:03:11.680
People like Joe Rogan, Colin Moriarty, Faisal
Saeed al Mutar, Bret Weinstein, Eric Weinstein,

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.150
Michael Shermer, Peter Boghossian and many
others offered strong defenses of me, just

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:19.880
as I've offered for others when I've seen
them unfairly attacked.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:23.550
I even got a public defense from Donald Trump
Jr.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:28.739
Putting my friends and public allies aside
though, it's incredibly inspiring and humbling

00:03:28.739 --> 00:03:34.430
to see literally 10's of thousands of people
offer their voice when they feel you've been

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.180
unjustly attacked.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.040
And that's the key to this whole thing.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.840
It's not me, or Sam, or Jordan or Bret that
they fear, what they really fear is that all

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:48.200
of you will starting saying what you think
... because There's strength in numbers.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.599
By Monday, I wanted to put the whole story
behind me.

00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:55.989
My dog has a health emergency, which helped
put everything in perspective, but I admit,

00:03:55.989 --> 00:03:59.270
I did get sucked back into the attack very
briefly.

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:04.690
Over the course of a Twitter exchange, I got
the writer of the piece, Josh Harkinson, to

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:09.580
publicly admit I am NOT further right than
Breitbart, though of course, he didn't change

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:13.450
the title or have Mother Jones issue any sort
of public correction.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:17.560
One other interesting piece to all this, is
that the writer, John Harkinson, is one of

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:24.419
the 40 people that James Hodgkinson, the shooter
of the Republican baseball team last week,

00:04:24.419 --> 00:04:25.860
followed on Twitter.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:31.650
Now I can't draw a direct link there, but
we know that Hodgkinson was a far lefty who

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.259
obviously was driven to political extremes.

00:04:34.259 --> 00:04:40.659
So, when this very same writer does a hatchet
job on me calling me further right than Breitbart,

00:04:40.659 --> 00:04:45.919
which is clearly code for racist, I cannot
sit back there and take it.

00:04:45.919 --> 00:04:49.460
This is exactly why I've been saying you can't
punch Nazi's.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:54.620
Call everyone you oppose a Nazi and a racist
and then eventually you will see violence

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.699
as the next logical step.

00:04:56.699 --> 00:05:02.060
It's not a crazy exercise to think that this
is partially what drove James Hodgkinson.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:06.139
In hindsight his attack on me was the next
obvious step in where this whole collectivist

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:07.139
movement is going.

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:12.810
I've talked for a long time about how if you
can't debate ideas, you use lies and buzzwords.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:16.259
Having it turned on me shouldn't have been
a surprise, especially from a Leftist site

00:05:16.259 --> 00:05:19.669
like Mother Jones, yet it still did surprise
me somehow.

00:05:19.669 --> 00:05:25.059
Make no mistake, there is a Thinkquisition
going on here, and it can come for anyone

00:05:25.059 --> 00:05:26.479
at any time.

00:05:26.479 --> 00:05:31.840
If you ally yourself with people who value
the movement, in this case a political one,

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:38.000
over you as an individual, then eventually
it is inevitable that they will come for you.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.900
And if they don't come for you, you're probably
the one coming for them.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:46.069
This Thinkquisition will come after anyone
who bucks the trend and the stereotypes and

00:05:46.069 --> 00:05:48.169
dares think for themselves.

00:05:48.169 --> 00:05:52.550
It's why they come accuse Ayaan Hirsi Ali
of being anti muslim, it's why they slander

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:57.039
Bill Maher as a being racist, it's why they
call Larry Elder an uncle tom, and it's why

00:05:57.039 --> 00:06:01.139
I can be branded a far right extremist.

00:06:01.139 --> 00:06:06.949
Those who are a part of this Thinkquisition
fear you thinking for yourself, that you won't

00:06:06.949 --> 00:06:10.809
bow to their collectivist demands, more than
anything else.

00:06:10.809 --> 00:06:16.020
The way to beat this witch hunt is to be yourself,
and fight for what you believe.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.600
You are the antidote they fear most.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:23.219
I hope that next time you see me fighting
back and getting some cover from my allies,

00:06:23.219 --> 00:06:28.210
it will inspire you to fight back... specifically
with words, not violence...

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:29.580
as well.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:34.310
Joining me on the show this week is one of
my aforementioned allies and friends, author

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:40.120
and professor Peter Boghossian, who will help
me dissect the madness of 2017 and much more.

